hadiths[41]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3561","It was narrated that Salamah bin Nufail Al-Kindi said:""I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah when a man said: 'O Messenger of Allah! The people have lost interest in horses and put down their weapons"
"3562","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is goodness tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection. And horses are of three types: Those that bring reward to man"
"3563","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah said:""Horses may bring reward to a man"
"3564","It was narrated that Anas said:""There was nothing dearer to the Messenger of Allah after women than horses"
"3565","It was narrated that Abu Wahb"
"3566","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:The Prophet used to dislike the Shikal among horses. And the wording is that of Isma'il"
"3567","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet used to dislike the Shikal among horses"
"3568","It was narrated from Salim"
"3569","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah said:""Omens are in houses"
"3570","It was narrated from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah said:""If there are (omens) in anything"
"3571","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Blessing is in the forelocks of horses"
"3572","It was narrated that Jarir said:""I saw the Messenger of Allah twisting the forelock of a horse with his two fingers"
"3573","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Prophet said:""There is goodness in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection"
"3574","It was narrated that 'Urwah Al-Bariqi said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection"
"3575","It was narrated from 'Urwah bin Abi Al-Ja'd that he heard the Prophet say:""Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection: Reward and spoils of war"
"3576","It was narrated that 'Urwah said that he heard the Messenger of Allah say:""Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection: Reward and spoils of war"
"3577","It was narrated from 'Urwah bin Abi Al-Ja'd that the Prophet said:""Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection: Reward and spoils of war"
"3578","It was narrated that Khalid bin Yazid Al-Juhani said:""Uqbah bin 'Amir used to pass by me and say: 'O Khalid"
"3579","It was narrated that Abu Dharr said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no Arabian horse but it is allowed to offer two supplications every Sahar (end of the night): O Allah"
"3580","It was narrated that Ali bin Abi Talib"
"3581","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Ubaidullah bin 'Abbas said:I was with Ibn 'Abbas and a man asked him: ""Did the Messenger of Allah recite during Zuhr and 'Asr?"" He said: ""No."" He said: ""Perhaps he used to recite to himself?"" He said: ""May your face be scratched! This question is worse than the first one. The Messenger of Allah was a slave whose Lord commanded him and he conveyed (the message). By Allah"
"3582","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah said:""Whoever keeps a horse for the cause of Allah out of faith in Allah and believing the promise of Allah"
"3583","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah organized a horse race and sent them from Al-Hafya' and its finish line was Thaniyyat Al-Wada'; and he organized a race for horses that had not been made lean"
"3584","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah organized a race for horses that had been made lean"
"3585","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah said:""There should be no awards (for victory in a competition) except for arrows"
"3586","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah said:""There should be no awards (for victory in a competition) except on arrows"
"3587","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""No award (for victory in a competition) is permissible except over camels or horses"
"3588","It was narrated that Anas said:""The Messenger of Allah had a she-camel called Al-'Adba' which could not be beaten. One day a Bedouin came on a riding-camel and beat her (in a race). The Muslims were upset by that"
"3589","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah said:""There should be no awards (for victory in a competition) except over camels or horses"
"3590","It was narrated from 'Imran bin Husain that the Messenger of Allah said:""There is no 'bringing'"
"3591","It was narrated from 'Imran bin Husain that the Messenger of Allah said:""There is no 'bringing'"
"3592","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""The Messenger of Allah raced with a Bedouin and (the latter) won. It was as if the Companions of the Messenger of Allah were upset by this"
"3593","It was narrated from Yahya bin 'Abbad bin 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair"
"3594","It was narrated that 'Amr bin Al-Harith said:""The Messenger of Allah did not leave behind a Dinar nor a Dirham"
"3595","Abu Ishaq narrated:""I heard 'Amr bin Al-Harith say: 'The Messenger of Allah did not leave behind anything except his white mule"
"3596","Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated that his father said:""I heard 'Amr bin Al-Harith say: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah and he left nothing behind except his white mule"
"3597","It was narrated from Sufyan Ath-Thawri"
"3598","A similar report was narrated from Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari"
"3599","It was narrated that Yazid -Ibn Ruzaiq- said:""Ibn 'Awn narrated to us"
"3600","It was narrated from Bishr"
"3601","It was narrated from Azhar As-Samman"